WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:04.685
Analysis moves from organized information to intelligence by explaining what the evidence

00:00:04.685 --> 00:00:05.995
means for the requirement.

00:00:05.995 --> 00:00:09.000
Begin with the observed record and create one or more hypotheses.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.190
A hypothesis is a testable explanation, not a conclusion to defend.

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:14.990
Develop competing explanations early.

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:18.995
For each one, identify expected evidence, contradictions, and missing information.

00:00:18.995 --> 00:00:23.175
This makes it harder to anchor on the first plausible story and then collect only material

00:00:23.175 --> 00:00:23.980
that confirms it.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:27.995
Pattern analysis can reveal recurring activity, timing, or shared characteristics.

00:00:27.995 --> 00:00:32.000
Link analysis can clarify documented relationships among entities and events.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.235
Neither technique proves intent by itself.

00:00:34.235 --> 00:00:39.000
Patterns may arise from common services, coincidence, incomplete data, or collection bias.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.995
Evaluate evidence according to relevance and reliability rather than volume.

00:00:42.995 --> 00:00:46.931
A single authenticated primary record may outweigh many recycled summaries.

00:00:46.931 --> 00:00:49.020
Record why evidence supports or weakens each explanation,

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:53.250
and preserve alternative interpretations where ambiguity remains.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:59.975
Identify gaps explicitly.

00:00:59.975 --> 00:01:01.010
Missing dates, uncertain identity, incomplete archives, language limitations,

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:01.970
or unavailable primary records can materially affect the judgment.

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:06.205
Absence of public evidence is not automatically evidence that something did not happen.

00:01:06.205 --> 00:01:09.000
Document the chain of reasoning from observations to judgments.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Use calibrated confidence and describe what could change the assessment.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Analytical discipline makes the result reviewable, correctable,

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.930
and useful without pretending that public information removes uncertainty.
